      "dcterms:title": "A CURIOUS q-ANALOGUE OF HERMITE POLYNOMIALS",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "CIGLER, JOHANN",
        "ZENG, JIANG"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20210709",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/0905.0228",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Two well-known q-Hermite polynomials are the continuous and discrete q-Hermite polynomials. In this paper we consider a new family of q-Hermite polynomials and prove several curious properties about these polynomials. One striking property is the connection with q-Fibonacci and q-Lucas polynomials. The latter relation yields a generalization of the Touchard-Riordan formula.",
